        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Deepen: one-word times",
        "body": "¿Qué aprendiste ayer sobre esta misma materia?\n\nEscribe aquí:\n____________________\n____________________\n____________________\n\n## Repaso\n\nOne word: canto / cantaba / canté / cantaré / cantaría.\n\nTwo words: helper haber + participle (he cantado).\n\nExplain one idea with your own words.\n\nToday we stay on **one-word** times only (no haber). Remember the thread: verb = action; conjugate = change for who and when; stem = fixed part; ending = tip. With those four ideas you can rebuild any simple form. This deepen day is your chance to hear the five clocks without the helper **haber** getting in the way. Walk the five clocks as one story: **canto** now, **cantaba** as open past, **canté** as closed past, **cantaré** ahead, **cantaría** as «would.» The helpful contrast is **cantaba** (leaves the moment open) versus **canté** (closes it). When I was little I **cantaba** in the shower every day; yesterday I **canté** once at the school concert—that night was finished.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Compare two short examples out loud. Say what changes and what stays the same. Write one sentence in your own words before you start the practice task.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Práctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Draw one clear symbol or small scene about “Practice one-word times”. Add one label from today's lesson.\n\nCommon mistake: Error común:\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Practice one-word times”. Add one label from today's lesson."
      }
    ],
